<type>[optional scope][!]: <description>

[optional body: explain what changed and why]

Project-Source: <plan|plan-task|task|prompt|manual>
Project-Plan: <.agents/plans/*.md or omit>
Project-Plan-Task: <plan task name or omit>
Project-Task: <TASKS.md T-AREA-NNN task ID/title or omit>
Project-Prompt: <short direct-request summary or omit>
Co-authored-by: <agent-name> <agent-email>
Refs: <paths/issues/ADRs or omit>
Validation: <command/result>

# Conventional Commits 1.0.0 shape:
#   <type>[optional scope][optional !]: <description>
#   [optional body]
#   [optional footer(s)]
#
# Repository types:
#   feat      new user-facing plugin behavior
#   fix       bug fix
#   docs      documentation-only change
#   test      test or manual sandbox validation change
#   refactor  internal code change with no behavior change
#   chore     repository maintenance
#   build     build, dependency, or tooling change
#   ci        CI or release automation change
#   perf      performance improvement
#   style     formatting-only change
#   revert    revert a previous commit
#
# Breaking changes:
#   Use ! or a BREAKING CHANGE: footer only when explicitly approved by user request,
#   accepted ADR, or accepted plan.
#
# Project metadata footers:
#   Project-Source is required for AI-created commits.
#   Co-authored-by footer is required for AI-created commits.
#   Keep all metadata footers contiguous; do not put blank lines between trailer lines.
#   Use plan for whole-plan or plan/spec-only commits.
#   Use plan-task for one named task within an active plan.
#   Use task for a TASKS.md item that is not covered by a plan.
#   Use prompt for a direct ad hoc user request.
#   Use manual only for human-authored commits outside the AI workflow.
#   Include only the Project-* footers that apply.
#   Validation is required for AI-created commits; say "not run" with a reason when needed.
#   For generated ADRs and plans, commit metadata supplements the artifact's context;
#   do not rely on the commit alone for decision or planning provenance.
#
# Examples:
#   docs(decisions): define all-files commit scope
#
#   Project-Source: prompt
#   Project-Prompt: define all files as every non-ignored committable change
#   Co-authored-by: <agent-name> <agent-email>
#   Refs: docs/decisions/0003-define-all-files-commit-scope.md
#   Validation: git diff --check - passed
#
#   build(scaffold): add IntelliJ plugin Gradle project
#   feat(commit): add AI Commit All split button
#   test(sandbox): add manual staging-area validation notes
